{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Elazar took.</b> Apparently this verse is not in its proper place; it should have written 'a memorial for the children of Israel' immediately after 'and they shall be for a sign for the children of Israel.' Rather, it was fixed here to create an interruption between them, and this teaches you that from the beginning of the passage until 'and they shall be for a sign for the children of Israel' it was said to Moshe to say to Elazar, and from 'a memorial for the children of Israel' until 'by the hand of Moshe' it was said to Moshe to say to Aharon. This is the meaning of 'as HaShem spoke by the hand of Moshe' — to him, to Aharon. And the proof is from the Sifrei: 'And HaShem spoke to Aharon — Behold I have given you etc.' — I might think 'speak to Aharon'; Scripture says 'a memorial for the children of Israel, that no foreigner draw near' — this teaches that the speech was to Moshe, to say to Aharon." "<b>Overlaid on the altar.</b> Until now it had no top."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The phrase ופי׳ כאשר דבר ביד משה לו לאהרן is read as explaining how the phrase כאשר דבר ה׳ ביד משה at the end of verse 5 is to be understood."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:21.781072374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}